      normal rather than a blip. The WorldFreightHub Europe route data puts sea transit at roughly
      <strong>30–38 days via the Cape of Good Hope</strong>, with the Red Sea reroute adding about
      <strong>+10–14 days</strong> versus the pre-crisis Suez routing. Rail from Xi\u2019an or Chengdu to
      the UK runs roughly <strong>18–25 days</strong>, with the Channel crossing adding time versus a
      continental terminus. UK air transit is not published, so that line stays explicit instead of
