      <h2>4. FCL vs LCL: which fits UK cargo?</h2>
      <p>
        The FCL-vs-LCL decision for the UK starts with cube, urgency and handling tolerance. FCL suits
        cargo large enough to justify a 20GP, 40GP or 40HQ; LCL suits smaller consignments sharing a
        container. A common planning split sits around <strong>15 CBM</strong> — below that LCL is usually
        cheaper, above it FCL starts to win — but that is a LOW-confidence heuristic, not a rate card, so
        request quotes on both sides before deciding.
      </p>

